# A captured Structure formal whose actual is another named type admitted by
# name with its fields permuted (D-105), read two levels deep (`m\box\c`): the
# first step through the admitted map, the second by Inner's own layout.
# 5 + 2 = 7; 81 is the program's own refusal.
Inner:
    int: c 5
end: Inner
Model:
    int: other 5
    box: Inner
    int: value 0
end: Model
Wide:
    int: value 0
    int: extra 9
    box: Inner
    int: other 5
end: Wide

fn: makeReader (Model: m) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: read (int: x) int
        return: m\box\c + x
    return: read

wide: merge: Wide
@: r makeReader(wide)
int: a (r: 2)
int: ok 7
if: a != 7
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
